@prefix gmeow:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/rights>
    a gmeow:Slice ;
    rdfs:label "rights"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "The rights slice of the GMEOW ontology (core tier): the cross-cutting, instance-level rights / IP / trademark / licensing facility — the machine-readable rights superset layer (ODRL, CC REL, dcterms, schema.org, RightsStatements.org, WIPO, SPDX, PREMIS). A licence IS a gmeow:Agreement (reusing gmeow:hasParty via gmeow:licensor / gmeow:licensee) and rights holders ARE agents (reusing gmeow:wasAttributedTo via gmeow:copyrightHolder / gmeow:trademarkHolder), never parallel party or holder models. Flat-first (gmeow:hasLicense / gmeow:hasCopyright) with reify-on-demand to the gmeow:RightsStatement relator bearing the ODRL-superset deontic trio (gmeow:Permission / gmeow:Prohibition / gmeow:Duty over open gmeow:RightsAction values), the constraint algebra, and conflict-resolution strategy. Licence families, action kinds, trademark and copyright statuses are OPEN value vocabularies with no primary right (Principle 9); licences and statuses are aligned to SPDX / RightsStatements.org IRIs by reference, never imported (Principle 5); expired / lapsed rights are suppressed, never deleted (Principle 10). Includes the privacy / consent / redaction facility, which reuses the deontic trio rather than minting a parallel consent relator. Distinct from the ontology-alignment license policy in config.py, which governs whether external AXIOMS may be copied into GMEOW. Anatomy, dependencies, and consumer are declared in this manifest; the manifest is the sole source of slice identity and tier."@x-gmeow-english ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/rights> ;
    dcterms:title "GMEOW Rights & IP Module"@x-gmeow-english ;
    dcterms:creator "Blackcat Informatics® Inc." ;
    gmeow:sliceTier gmeow:tierCore ;
    gmeow:sliceDependsOn
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/agreements> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/kernel> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/observations> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/provenance> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/creative-works> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/documents> ,
        <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/names> ;
    gmeow:sliceConsumer "Licensing and rights of every artifact across the ontology: GMEOW's own dual licence, the Images super-ontology, software (SPDX / SBOM exports via gmeow:spdxLicenseId), and the mail corpus; the Employment / publication block; generated machine-readable projections (queries/projections/odrl.rq, cc.rq, schema-org.rq) for ODRL policies, CC REL licences, and the schema.org rights cluster; public-facing licence, copyright-notice, attribution, and trademark surfaces (schema.org JSON-LD, Wikidata); and the privacy / consent / redaction facility driving disclosure control over personal data."@x-gmeow-english .
